#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:5
#: 4a36313382fa4dcfb3888b798107d0df
msgid "Tuning Turn Rate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:7
#: ee4d53b3f909401dbfd3bbdae6d2e924
msgid "This page describes how a Rover's Turn Rate controller (aka steering rate controller) can be tuned.  This is the most important controller to tune in order to achieve good steering control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:13
#: 487d8b40efd040298f593bd2522abd7c
msgid "Turn Rate PID Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:15
#: 99297e009c3f4a3ab110784dc80fb7a6
msgid "The Turn Rate controller attempts to achieve the desired turn rate (set by the pilot or autopilot) using a PID controller.  All modes except :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>` and :ref:`Manual <manual-mode>` use this controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:17
#: 900f29fc959e4e0399652186aabf643e
msgid "The FF, P, I and D gains for this controller are held in the :ref:`ATC_STR_RAT_FF <ATC_STR_RAT_FF>`, :ref:`ATC_STR_RAT_P <ATC_STR_RAT_P>`, :ref:`ATC_STR_RAT_I <ATC_STR_RAT_I>` and :ref:`ATC_STR_RAT_D <ATC_STR_RAT_D>` parameters respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:19
#: 1c478ce65d4d408880805c7d7febd3ae
msgid "Recommended steps for tuning this controller are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:21
#: 7e323cc137e14d3b83a332d25692e077
msgid "Connect the ground station to the vehicle using a telemetry radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:22
#: 803e910627ad4f2bbd0966887d02b2c6
msgid "Set the :ref:`ACRO_TURN_RATE <ACRO_TURN_RATE>` parameter to be roughly what the vehicle's maximum turn rate is in deg/sec.  For a more precise measurement:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:24
#: dc39b7d158ac43f6bd8fec377c81ad44
msgid "On Mission Planner's Flight Data screen, check the \"Tuning\" checkbox (bottom middle), double click on the graph and select \"gz\" (Gyro Z-axis)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:25
#: 52cc88cb70ee4ba092670cd30fb860f3
msgid "Drive the vehicle in Manual mode at a medium speed making very sharp turns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:26
#: e2b5fe68a612420d81ad135a51ef3400
msgid "Set :ref:`ACRO_TURN_RATE <ACRO_TURN_RATE>` to a bit lower than the highest values seen.  Note the value shown may be in centi-degrees/sec so its value should be divided by 100 to match the parameter's deg/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:28
#: ad83da028e8549b6bb84c153dcbc4f64
msgid "Set the :ref:`GCS_PID_MASK <GCS_PID_MASK>` to 1 (Steering)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:29
#: a4c002dff89546168eeba8ad1e6f91b7
msgid "On Mission Planner's Flight Data screen, check the \"Tuning\" checkbox (bottom middle), double click on the graph and select \"pidachieved\", \"piddesired\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:34
#: 52bff47e8b3c407e94ce679f1aeb5ffc
msgid "Drive the vehicle in :ref:`Acro <acro-mode>` at a medium speed making various wide and tight turns and compare how well pidachieved follows piddesired"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:35
#: a16b829fcaff4c98ab1dca849188cbf4
msgid "Tune the :ref:`FF gain <ATC_STR_RAT_FF>` first.  This gain converts the desired turn rate directly into a steering servo or motor output.  If the vehicle's turn rate response is sluggish then this parameter should be increased.  If the vehicle is constantly overshooting its desired turn rate then this parameter should be reduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:36
#: 3986a9abce3c4a7eb55b41fc375b7ebe
msgid "The :ref:`P gain <ATC_STR_RAT_P>` corrects for short-term error.  It can often be set to a low value (e.g. 20% of FF) if the FF value is set well.  If set too high the turn rate may oscillate.  This :ref:`P gain <ATC_STR_RAT_P>` should always be lower than the :ref:`FF gain <ATC_STR_RAT_FF>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:37
#: a30d9e9880384c73bf720ed0ed1be982
msgid "The :ref:`I gain <ATC_STR_RAT_I>` corrects for long-term error.  It can often be set to the same value as P.  If the vehicle never achieves the desired turn rate, then this parameter should be increased.  If the vehicle's turn rate slowly oscillates then this parameter should be reduced.  This :ref:`I gain <ATC_STR_RAT_I>` should always be lower than then :ref:`FF gain <ATC_STR_RAT_FF>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:38
#: 4c9fd5b6b6c74fb5a120608fd1a72bd7
msgid "The :ref:`D gain <ATC_STR_RAT_D>` is meant to stabilize the output by fighting against short-term changes in turn rate.  This gain can normally be left at zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:40
#: b5d56b04205b40a8b2c4134da3ad17ac
msgid "Finally set :ref:`ATC_STR_RAT_MAX <ATC_STR_RAT_MAX>` to the :ref:`ACRO_TURN_RATE <ACRO_TURN_RATE>` value and optionally reduce :ref:`ACRO_TURN_RATE <ACRO_TURN_RATE>`.  The difference between these two parameters is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:42
#: 3316cbbcd2c749e889741cb775708738
msgid ":ref:`ACRO_TURN_RATE <ACRO_TURN_RATE>` controls how the pilot's input is converted to a desired turn rate in Acro mode.  This parameter can be reduced to make turns in Acro mode more docile for the driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-steering-rate.rst:43
#: 0c13134a4b9a49e099ae54fcf78bc5b5
msgid ":ref:`ATC_STR_RAT_MAX <ATC_STR_RAT_MAX>` is the maximum turn rate that the vehicle will ever attempt in any mode.  This should normally be kept close to the vehicle's performance limits so the vehicle remains agile"
msgstr ""

